@startuml ActiveConsent

title Inquiry Active Consent API Sequence

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Consent Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_consent" as t_consent
    database "m_consent_type" as m_consent_type
end box
user -> page: Request current public consents
activate page
page -> api: GET v1/consent/active (timestamp, requestId)
activate api
api -> app: [**InquiryActiveConsentQueryHandler**] Process request
activate app
app -> app: Generate requestId if omitted; validate mandatory UTC timestamp
note over app, infra
    There is no body or query parameter. Validate mandatory timestamp as a UTC timestamp before SQL;
    missing/malformed value returns 400 E10001 before a transaction. Generate requestId when omitted. Only
    public consent definitions are returned; no user evidence, credential or assignment data is read or exposed.
end note
alt Missing or malformed timestamp
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Header validation error
else Valid request
    app -> infra: BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
    note over app, infra
        This makes consent/type visibility and the mandatory type name consistent when another request edits or
        deactivates a type between queries. Do not substitute transaction-start NOW() or the caller's timestamp for
        the server-captured eligibility time. No locking SELECT or data write is needed.
        COMMIT the read-only transaction before 200. Timeout before commit rolls back and returns 408 E90001; an
        unexpected pre-commit failure (including incomplete mapping) rolls back and returns generic 500 without a
        new bizCode. All SQL results return to Application before deriving ids, mapping fields or responding.
    end note
    alt Read-only work completes
        app -> app: Capture server UTC now immediately before first query; establish snapshot
        app -> infra: QUERY - Get active consents
        infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get active consents
        activate t_consent
            note right of t_consent
                SELECT
                    c.id as consent_id,
                    c.code,
                    c.consent_type_id,
                    c.consent_version,
                    c.consent_name,
                    c.consent_description,
                    c.effective_at,
                    c.expired_at,
                    c.is_required,
                    c.body
                FROM consent.t_consent c
                WHERE c.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                AND c.effective_at <= '<sequence.now>'
                AND (c.expired_at IS NULL OR c.expired_at > '<sequence.now>')
                AND EXISTS (
                    SELECT 1
                    FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                    WHERE ct.id = c.consent_type_id
                    AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                )
                ORDER BY c.effective_at, c.id
            end note
            t_consent -> infra: Return ordered visibleConsents (current fields and type ids)
        deactivate t_consent
        infra -> app: Return ordered visibleConsents (current fields and type ids)
        alt visibleConsents is empty
            app -> app: data.consents = []; skip type-name lookup
        else visibleConsents is non-empty
            app -> app: consentTypeIds = distinct visibleConsents.consent_type_id
            app -> infra: QUERY - Get consent type
            infra -> m_consent_type: QUERY - Get consent type
            activate m_consent_type
                note right of m_consent_type
                    SELECT
                        ct.id as consent_type_id,
                        ct.name as consent_type_name
                    FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                    WHERE ct.id = ANY ('<sequence.consentTypeIds>'::UUID[])
                    AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    ORDER BY ct.id
                end note
                m_consent_type -> infra: Return ACTIVE type names by typeId
            deactivate m_consent_type
            infra -> app: Return ACTIVE type names by typeId
            app -> domain: Merge eleven public fields; require every consentTypeName; preserve nulls and current versions
            domain -> app: Return complete data.consents in effective_at ASC, id ASC order
            app -> app: Mapping failure throws before COMMIT; use unexpected-failure path
        end
        app -> infra: COMMIT
        infra -> app: Return completed read-only transaction
        note over app, infra
            Hide a consent whose type is not ACTIVE even when the consent itself is ACTIVE/effective. This detailed
            endpoint revision remains in-review; no backend implementation is included.
            Include a consent starting exactly at now and exclude one expiring exactly at now.
            INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED/DELETED types are hidden. The pending/registration/submission APIs apply the same
            target visibility rule in their own reviews.
            Return every visible current consent, including both required and optional ones. isRequired comes from
            c.is_required, not the type's default. The endpoint has no user-specific pending/acceptance filter. Do not
            expose hidden consents as a fallback for a missing type name.
            For a non-empty list, derive consentTypeIds from the returned rows and fetch their ACTIVE type names with a
            typed UUID array in the same snapshot. Map all eleven response fields: consentId, code, consentTypeId,
            consentTypeName, consentVersion, consentName, consentDescription, effectiveAt, expiredAt, isRequired and
            body. Nullable description/expiry stay null; do not invent default values or a version.
            Every returned consent must resolve its mandatory consentTypeName. The query's ACTIVE-type filter and the
            same snapshot's name lookup guarantee this mapping. Missing mapping is an internal consistency failure that
            rolls back and returns generic 500, never partial success. A type deactivated after this snapshot is absent
            in the next request; the current response consistently reflects its established snapshot.
            When no visible consent exists, skip the type-name lookup and return 200 S10000 with data.consents=[] after
            COMMIT. An empty list is never 404. UUID arrays and timestamps are typed bound parameters, not interpolated
            SQL.
            This GET never records reading or acceptance and never inserts/updates/deletes data. The client keeps the
            displayed current version for its later register/submit request; those endpoints record the user's
            displayed/read state separately. No cookie, session or user-specific state changes on this inquiry.
        end note
        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Active Consent Success; data.consents
        api -> page: Return ordered list or [] without creating user evidence
        page -> user: Display current definitions and retain displayed versions
    else Timeout before COMMIT
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
        api -> page: Inquiry timed out
    else Unexpected pre-commit failure including incomplete mapping
        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
        app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
        api -> page: Generic inquiry failure
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
